<main class="flex-1 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-14">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold mb-2">Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mb-10">Last updated: <%= new Date().toISOString().slice(0,10) %> &middot; Placeholder template &mdash; have a lawyer review before you go live.</p>

  <div class="space-y-8 text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">

    <section class="rounded-xl bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 p-5">
      <h2 class="font-bold text-amber-900 mb-2">Please read this section first</h2>
      <p class="text-amber-900">
        <%= site.name %> sells social-media marketing (SMM) services: followers, likes, views, comments
        and similar engagement for Instagram accounts and posts. These services are fulfilled through
        third-party providers and are generally understood to conflict with
        <a href="https://help.instagram.com/477434105621119" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="underline">Instagram/Meta's own Terms of Use and Community Guidelines</a>,
        which prohibit buying or selling fake engagement and using third-party apps to inflate metrics.
        Using these services can lead to removed followers/likes, reduced reach, feature
        restrictions, or account suspension by Instagram &mdash; entirely at Instagram's discretion and
        outside our control. By creating an account and placing an order you confirm you understand
        and accept this risk for yourself.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base mb-2">1. Who we are / acceptance of terms</h2>
      <p>These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of <%= site.name %> (the "Service"). By registering an
        account or placing an order you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the Service.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base mb-2">2. Eligibility</h2>
      <p>You must be at least 18 years old, or the age of majority in your jurisdiction, and legally able to
        enter into a binding contract to use the Service. You are responsible for the account(s) and
        links you submit, and must only submit content/links you are authorised to promote.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base mb-2">3. Orders, pricing &amp; wallet</h2>
      <p>Prices are shown per 1,000 units and may change at any time; the price shown at the moment you
        place an order is the price charged. Funds are held in an in-app wallet. Wallet top-ups are
        reviewed manually and credited once confirmed &mdash; see the
        <a href="/refund-policy" class="text-brand-700 underline">Refund Policy</a> for cancellation and
        refund conditions.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base mb-2">4. Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You may not use the Service to target: accounts or content you don't own or have permission to
        promote; content that is illegal, promotes violence or hate, is sexually exploitative of minors,
        infringes someone else's rights, or is otherwise prohibited by applicable law. We reserve the
        right to refuse, cancel or refund any order that violates this section, and to suspend accounts
        that abuse the Service.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base mb-2">5. No guarantee against platform action</h2>
      <p>We do not control Instagram/Meta's enforcement systems. We do not guarantee that delivered
        engagement will remain on your account permanently, that your account will not be flagged,
        limited or suspended, or that any specific algorithmic outcome (reach, follows, sales) will
        result from using the Service.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base mb-2">6. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>The Service is provided "as is". To the maximum extent permitted by law, <%= site.name %> is not
        liable for indirect, incidental or consequential damages, including loss of followers, account
        suspension, lost business, or lost profits arising from use of the Service. Our total liability
        for any claim is limited to the amount you paid for the order giving rise to the claim.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base mb-2">7. Account suspension &amp; termination</h2>
      <p>We may suspend or terminate accounts that violate these Terms, engage in fraud or chargebacks,
        or abuse the Service. You may stop using the Service and close your account at any time by
        contacting <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-700 underline">support</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base mb-2">8. Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>We may update these Terms from time to time. Continued use of the Service after changes take
        effect constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base mb-2">9. Governing law</h2>
      <p>[Fill in: the governing law / jurisdiction for your business.] &mdash; replace this bracket with
        your actual governing law clause once you've registered your business.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="font-bold text-gray-900 text-base mb-2">10. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these Terms? Reach us via the <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-700 underline">contact page</a>.</p>
    </section>

  </div>
</main>

